herwise-empty band; c2 (267) likewise represents detailed alone over its share (32)\",\n     3\t  \"fixture\": \"derived-thread\",\n     4\t  \"params\": { \"lowerBound\": 400, \"percentages\": { \"full\": 25, \"smooth\": 7, \"detailed\": 8, \"brief\": 60 } },\n     5\t  \"compactPoint\": 48,\n     6\t  \"coveredFrom\": 1,\n     7\t  \"arrangement\": [\n     8\t    { \"band\": \"brief\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c1\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_brief\", \"degraded\": false },\n     9\t    { \"band\": \"detailed\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c2\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_detailed\", \"degraded\": false },\n    10\t    { \"band\": \"smooth\", \"subjectKind\": \"turn\", \"subjectId\": \"t8\", \"formUsed\": \"turn_rendering\", \"degraded\": false }\n    11\t  ],\n    12\t  \"gaps\": []\n    13\t}\npackages/lhc/test/goldens/g4-turnless-straggler.json\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"case\": \"G4 turnless straggler: the between-turns note attaches to t4 and rides c2's band entry; the trailing note is tail by construction\",\n     3\t  \"fixture\": \"straggler-variant\",\n     4\t  \"params\": { \"lowerBound\": 400, \"percentages\": { \"full\": 25, \"smooth\": 16, \"detailed\": 10, \"brief\": 49 } },\n     5\t  \"compactPoint\": 49,\n     6\t  \"coveredFrom\": 1,\n     7\t  \"arrangement\": [\n     8\t    { \"band\": \"brief\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c1\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_brief\", \"degraded\": false },\n     9\t    { \"band\": \"detailed\", \"subjectKind\": \"chunk\", \"subjectId\": \"c2\", \"formUsed\": \"chunk_summary_detailed\", \"degraded\": false },\n    10\t    { \"band\": \"smooth\", \"subjectKind\": \"turn\", \"subjectId\": \"t7\", \"formUsed\": \"turn_rendering\", \"degraded\": false },\n    11\t    { \"band\": \"smooth\", \"subjectKind\": \"turn\", \"subjectId\": \"t8\", \"formUsed\": \"turn_rendering\", \"degraded\": false }\n    12\t  ],\n    13\t  \"gaps\": []\n    14\t}\npackages/lhc/test/goldens/README.md\n     1\t# Selection goldens (Epic 03 Story 2, G1–G4)\n     2\t\n     3\tCommitted expected arrangements for the band-selection walk (tech design\n     4\t§Deterministic Algorithms), consumed by `test/view-select-golden.test.ts`.\n     5\tEach golden pins the exact arrangement a compact must produce on the Story-0\n     6\tfixture (or its straggler variant) under explicit params: subject ids per\n     7\tband, form used, compact point, covered_from, and gaps.\n     8\t\n     9\t**Goldens are immutable once committed.** An implementation that disagrees\n    10\twith a golden is wrong until the *design rule* is shown wrong — that takes the\n    11\tdeviation process, not a golden edit. The expected values were hand-derived\n    12\tfrom the design's rules (rules 1–6, the pinned ≤/newest-first/newest-member\n    13\ttie-breakers) against the fixture's deterministic token costs.\n    14\t\n    15\tRegenerated once under impl-lead ruling\n    16\t`02-smart-compact-story-run-001-ruling-013`: the first commit's goldens\n    17\tencoded extra-rule selection behavior (smooth-obligate inclusion,\n    18\tpartial-chunk retreat, suppressed brief loner); these goldens encode the\n    19\tliteral rules.\n    20\t\n    21\t| File | Case | Rule under test |\n    22\t|------|------|-----------------|\n    23\t| `g1-proportions.json` | G1 | shares → bands across the full gradient |\n    24\t| `g2-edge-inclusion.json` | G2a | entry exactly filling the remainder is included (≤) |\n    25\t| `g2-edge-exclusion.json` | G2b | one token under the exact fill → excluded, band stops |\n    26\t| `g3-oversized-loner.json` | G3 | oversized entry on an otherwise-empty band represents alone |\n    27\t| `g4-turnless-straggler.json` | G4 | rule 6: straggler rides the following turn's band entry; trailing straggler is tail |\n    28\t\n    29\t## Regeneration (only with a granted deviation)\n    30\t\n    31\tThe actual arrangement for any params can be printed by running the golden\n    32\tsuite with `GOLDEN_DUMP=1`:\n    33\t\n    34\t```\n    35\tGOLDEN_DUMP=1 npx vitest run test/view-select-golden.test.ts\n    36\t```\n    37\t\n    38\tEach case logs its actual `{compactPoint, coveredFrom, arrangement, gaps}`\n    39\tJSON; verify the new values against the design rules by hand before replacing\n    40\ta file, and record the deviation that made the old golden wrong.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
